firm_constitution:
You are preparing a Detailed Project Report (DPR) for bank loan purposes.

Generate the section exactly in the following structure and format:

Title:
"Constitution of the Firm"

First write one short paragraph describing the firm and ownership.

Then provide bullet points in this format, choosing exactly ONE person label based on {{organisation_type}}:

• Firm Name            : {{firm_name}}
• Constitution         : {{organisation_type}}
• Sector               : {{sector}}
• Nature of Business   : {{nature_of_business}}
• Person Name          : {{proprietor_name}}
• PAN No.              : {{pan_number}}
• Aadhar No.           : {{aadhar_number}}
• Caste                : {{caste}}
• Residential Address  : {{residential_address}}

For the Person Name label, output the correct label instead of the generic label above:
- Sole proprietorship: "Proprietor Name"
- Partnership firm: "Partner Name"
- LLP: "Partner Name"
- Private limited company: "Director Name"
- Public limited company: "Director Name"
- Any other constitution: "Member Name"
For multiple partners, directors, or members, include the corresponding names without describing a company director as a proprietor.

Rules:
- Use only the above structure.
- Maintain exact labels and spacing before colon.
- Do not add extra headings, tables, or explanations.
- Language must be formal and suitable for bank DPR.
- Residential Address is optional. The Residential Address must be entered manually by the user and must not be auto-populated from the Unit/Business Address in General Information. If PAN No., Aadhar No., or Residential Address is blank, omit that bullet. Do not invent an identifier or an address, and do not copy the unit or business address into Residential Address.
- If either or both of PAN No. and Aadhar No. are missing, leave the missing identifier out of the report entirely: omit its bullet, do not mention it in the paragraph, and do not write "Not provided", "N/A", or any placeholder for it.

promoter_details:
You are preparing a Detailed Project Report (DPR) for bank loan purposes.

Selected Sector: {{sector}}
Sector is exactly one of: Manufacturing, Trading, Service with Stock, Service without Stock.
Nature of Business: {{nature_of_business}}

Use the following proprietor / promoter data. It must contain separate details for every person:
{{promoter_list_bullets}}

Promoter ages (one age per person, matched to the same person's name): {{promoter_ages}}

Additional promoter data, if supplied:
- Name: {{proprietor_name}}
- Designation: {{designation}}
- Education: {{education_background}}
- Previous Experience: {{experience_details}}
- Caste/Category: {{caste}}
- PAN Number: {{pan_number}}
- Aadhaar Number: {{aadhar_number}}
- Residential Address: {{proprietor_address}}
- Share Ratio: {{share_ratio}}
- Title hint: {{promoter_title}}

Choose the title using the firm's legal constitution:
- Sole proprietorship: "Proprietor's Background"
- Partnership firm or LLP: "Partner's Background"
- Private limited company or public limited company: "Director's Background"
- Any other constitution: "Member's Background"
Use {{promoter_title}} only when consistent with this mapping.

Write one detailed professional paragraph for each person, with each person's description in a separate paragraph. Describe that person's qualifications, detailed experience, role, and ability to contribute to the proposed business. Include age, designation, share ratio, and other supplied details where relevant. Never combine different people's details into one paragraph or assign one person's experience to another. Use only supplied facts.

Then provide a table with one row per person:

| Name | PAN | Aadhaar | Residential Address | Sharing Ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| <person-specific values from the supplied promoter data> |

Then provide a separate experience table, with one row per person and a detailed experience description:

| Name | Age | Previous / Industry Experience | Qualification |
|---|---|---|---|
| <person name> | <that person's age> | <that person's detailed experience> | <that person's qualification> |

Rules:
- Include every person represented in {{promoter_list_bullets}}; do not show only the first person.
- Keep each person's experience separate and detailed, using the experience data supplied for that person.
- Show each person's share ratio. If the supplied share ratio is a combined ratio such as 50:50, assign its components to the listed people in the same order only when the number of components matches the number of people; display each person's percentage separately. Never invent or assume an unspecified ratio.
- Use the age corresponding to each person from {{promoter_ages}} and the promoter data. Do not invent missing ages.
- Do not invent qualifications, experience, PAN/Aadhaar numbers, addresses, or ownership details.
- Use formal banking report language and do not add unrelated headings or explanations.

